---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="System Architect at ExxonMobil, based in Bangkok, Thailand"
	pubDate={new Date('August 08 2021')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		I'm a System Architect at ExxonMobil in Bangkok, Thailand, with a background spanning backend
		development, software architecture, and data platform design. Over the past seven years I've
		grown from an intern building chatbots and front-end interfaces into an architect shaping how
		large-scale systems and data platforms are built.
	</p>

	<p>
		Since early 2024, I've been working in Data Analytics, designing and implementing a new data
		ingestion strategy for the foundation layer. I architect scalable, standardized ingest patterns
		using Snowflake as the enterprise data warehouse, with ETL pipelines built on Qlik and Azure
		Data Factory (ADF). I've established data modeling, transformation, and governance standards to
		keep pipelines consistent, reliable, and performant, and I work closely with cross-functional
		teams to align architecture with business analytics needs and long-term data strategy.
	</p>

	<p>
		From late 2021 to early 2024, I was a Software System Architect, leading the design and
		evolution of system architecture for scalability, performance, and long-term maintainability. I
		defined architectural standards, reviewed technical designs, and guided the team in building
		robust microservices-based solutions, providing technical leadership across backend development
		(Java Spring Boot), infrastructure, and deployment.
	</p>

	<p>
		I started at ExxonMobil in 2019 as a Back End Developer, building and maintaining RESTful APIs
		with Java and Spring Boot, and contributing to DevOps and Infrastructure as Code initiatives
		using Terraform to support CI/CD and cloud infrastructure management. Before that, I interned as
		a Front-End Web Developer (Vue.js, Angular) and a Chatbot Developer, and worked as a Teaching
		Assistant for Introduction to Computer Science at Kasetsart University, helping students learn
		Python and fundamental algorithms.
	</p>
</Layout>
